<article class="env-lemma" id="05HK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05HK">Lemma <span data-tag="05HK">38.5.4</span>.</a> Let $S$, $X$, $\mathcal{F}$, $x$, $s$ be as in Definition <a href="/tag/05HI" data-tag="05HI">38.5.2</a>. Let $(S', s') \to (S, s)$ be a morphism of pointed schemes which induces an isomorphism $\kappa (s) = \kappa (s')$. Let $(Z_ k, Y_ k, i_ k, \pi _ k, \mathcal{G}_ k, \alpha _ k, z_ k, y_ k)_{k = 1, \ldots , n}$ be a complete dévissage of $\mathcal{F}/X/S$ at $x$. Let $(Z'_ k, Y'_ k, i'_ k, \pi '_ k, \mathcal{G}'_ k, \alpha '_ k)_{k = 1, \ldots , n}$ be as constructed in Lemma <a href="/tag/05HJ" data-tag="05HJ">38.5.3</a> and let $x' \in X'$ (resp. $z'_ k \in Z'$, $y'_ k \in Y'$) be the unique point mapping to both $x \in X$ (resp. $z_ k \in Z_ k$, $y_ k \in Y_ k$) and $s' \in S'$. If $S'$ is affine, then $(Z'_ k, Y'_ k, i'_ k, \pi '_ k, \mathcal{G}'_ k, \alpha '_ k, z'_ k, y'_ k)_{k = 1, \ldots , n}$ is a complete dévissage of $\mathcal{F}'/X'/S'$ at $x'$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Lemma <a href="/tag/05HJ" data-tag="05HJ">38.5.3</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/05H8" data-tag="05H8">38.4.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>